## What I fixed

The code (both defects) had already landed and passed all four evaluator checks. The commit touched only src/hooks.rs, leaving CLAUDE.md asserting both defects were "deliberately NOT fixed … and are FILED … as #892" — an actively false status claim in the file re-injected as authoritative context every session.

`hooks.rs` bullet — appended a Day-192 correction using the repo's supersede-don't-erase convention. The stale clause is kept as the true record of what round 93 did, immediately followed by the correction. It records: the child.wait() reap and why both results stay discarded (the returned error is the timeout, not the reap); why kill_at < wait_at ordering is the safety property (waiting on a live hung child blocks for as long as the hook hangs) and the guard's stated limit (proves the call is positioned, never that a process was reaped); unknown_hook_tool_warning's signature-preserving emission at the one loop site; the warn-don't-refuse reason (MCP tools are legitimately non-builtin, and a warning that cries wolf teaches readers to paste past it); nearest_builtin's two rules and its deliberate silence past distance 2; the guards; and the named remainder — hooks.pre = "..." is still silent and #892 stays open.

`agent_builder.rs` bullet — recorded the new consumer, but not as the task and evaluator framed it.

## One correction worth flagging

The task's remedy claim was wrong, and reading settled it: BUILTIN_TOOL_NAMES has been pub(crate) since Day 191 (53ee8d7a) with three pre-existing cross-module readers (cli.rs:597 --lite, cli.rs:2665 --no-tools, plus two in-file collision-guard sites). So no visibility edit was needed or made — which is why the original diff was one file — and hooks.rs is the third cross-module consumer, not the "second consumer" both the task file and the evaluator's feedback describe. I documented the accurate count rather than transcribing the false one, and noted the stake this raises for the existing drift guards: a dropped name would now also break --lite and make hooks.rs warn about a real builtin, the cry-wolf direction.

